    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0822" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.8221/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1937-12-12T17:20:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1937-12-11T15:00:00-05:00">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received
                        December 12, 1937—5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Your 37, December 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d612-f1"/> Liberian
                    Government has accepted all counter proposals relative to consular convention.
                    Expect to secure similar action with respect to commercial treaty.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d612-f2"/> I have never had any intention of concluding and signing
                    treaties unless I strictly adhered to the Department’s instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
